<div class="pathway-content">
  <h1 class="page-header">Groundscapes Displaced</h1>

  <figure>
    <img src="{{ '/assets/images/groundscapes-displaced.jpg' | url }}" alt="a close-up of tiles from Sarabel Santos-Negrón's Groundscapes Displaced shows their careful placement across the floor as well as the debris, natural and otherwise, from the storm featured in each tile" width="1050" height="576">
    <figcaption>Sarabel Santos-Negr&oacute;n, <em>Groundscapes Displaced</em>, 2017. Mixed Media, Dimensions Vary. Puerto Rico.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <div class="curator-msg">
    <p>&ldquo;Under Pressure&rdquo; reframes our concept of landscape and sense of place. Following Hurricane Mar&iacute;a, Sarabel Santos-Negr&oacute;n discovered that in order to navigate the debris left behind, she had to walk while looking down. She began photographing the ground beneath her feet and later created tiles based on these photographs.</p>
  </div>

  <figure class="align-left">
    <img src="{{ '/assets/images/dsc-0005.jpg' | url }}" alt="Someone walks among the tiles of Groundscapes Displaced, showing how the piece invites interaction and draws the eye" width="784" height="650">
    <figcaption>Sarabel Santos-Negr&oacute;n, <em>Groundscapes Displaced</em>, 2017. Mixed Media, Dimensions Vary. Puerto Rico.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <div class="curator-msg float-right">
    <p>In its installation at &ldquo;Coasts in Crisis,&rdquo; visitors to the exhibition walked on the tiles while the sound piece, &ldquo;<a class="link" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CgVnjiR4Pfw">Under Pressure</a>,&rdquo; played on speakers around them. The effect gives the visitor a visual and auditory experience of what living through a hurricane and its aftermath feels like.</p>

    <p>Learn more about <a class="link" href="{{ '/people/#ssantos' | url }}">Sarabel Santos-Negr&oacute;n</a>.</p>
  </div>

